.TH SWAYDESK-LOCK 1 2026-11-14 "swaydesk 0.1.8" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-lock \- lock screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-lock
.br
.B swaydesk\-lock
\-\-notify\-fd N
.br
.B swaydesk\-lock
\-\-blur
.SH DESCRIPTION
The lock screen, through ext\-session\-lock\-v1 (gtk4\-layer\-shell 1.2 or newer).
.PP
Run with no arguments, it locks the screen through the package's sway\-lock helper (bin/../libexec/swaydesk, bin/../lib/swaydesk, or its own folder in the dotfiles; never the PATH or the home folder) and exits with its code: 0 as soon as the screen is locked, or if it was already locked, without starting a second lock; any other code means nothing locked. It does not wait for the unlock, like
.BR "swaylock \-f" ,
so it suits a key binding and swayidle's timeout and before\-sleep alike. Without the sway\-lock helper (shipped in the swaydesk\-lock package itself), it exits 1 and names the places it looked in.
.PP
The sway\-lock helper starts it with \-\-notify\-fd through its supervisor, which falls back to the lock in Python (sway\-lock\-gtk, on Debian and Ubuntu) and then to gtklock if it fails, and hands the lock to another locker if it exits without unlocking. The password field is on every monitor, takes dead keys through GTK's simple input method (never an input method daemon), and PAM checks the password with the swaydesk\-lock service.
.PP
Without the lock support in gtk4\-layer\-shell, it exits 1 and sway\-lock uses the next locker.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the usage and exit 0. Any other argument prints the usage and exits 2.
.TP
.B \-\-notify\-fd N
Write L to the file descriptor N when locked, F if another client already locked, and U after the unlock.
.TP
.B \-\-blur
Generate the blurred background of each monitor in advance (also when run as sway\-lock\-blur); without Sway or a wallpaper, do nothing and exit 0.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit 0 if the installed gtk4\-layer\-shell supports locking, 1 if not.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/swaydesk-lock
The PAM service used to check the password (only \fBauth include login\fR, like swaylock's). Without it, the
swaylock service, \fI/etc/pam.d/swaylock\fR, is used.
.TP
.I ~/.config/swaydesk/config.toml
The desktop configuration: language, accent color, GTK and icon themes, folder color, file manager, weather location and holidays.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pam (8),
.BR swaydesk (7),
.BR gtklock (1)
